  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Notoamide B may interact with VMRC-MELG through a series of target relationships. Specifically, Notoamide B is linked to Malme-3M, which is a target of 2-(1a,4-dimethyl-3,3a,4,5,6,7,7a,7b-octahydro-2H-naphtho[1,2-b]oxiren-7-yl)prop-2-enoic acid, and this compound further targets VMRC-MELG. Similarly, Notoamide B is also linked to A498, which is a target of Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-, and this compound also targets VMRC-MELG. These findings indicate that Notoamide B may act through multiple pathways to influence VMRC-MELG, potentially through different molecular mechanisms. The evidence suggests a possible role for Notoamide B in modulating VMRC-MELG, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the biological relevance of these interactions.",
